},$\n\n- the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ is an estimator of the population mean $\\mu ,$ and\n\n- the value $\\overset{^}{\\mu }=\\overset{¯}{x}$ is an estimate of the population mean $\\mu .$\n\nTherefore, our estimate for the population mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{\\mu } & =\\overset{―}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{6}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(4-7+6-3+5-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{6} \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-05770093-228f-5a71-80b2-0c344bf688cf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-05770093-228f-5a71-80b2-0c344bf688cf" :answer-field/id #uuid "05770093-228f-5a71-80b2-0c344bf688cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1dd3b9ac-3e11-5981-a4d8-309f740a2b9a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1dd3b9ac-3e11-5981-a4d8-309f740a2b9a" "answer-0c9718c7-902f-5345-ad03-482984e9c1fe" "answer-ea847776-7f1b-5b89-bb47-fd8b7fc0ef23" "answer-635832eb-ba37-5e03-b2a0-da170625a38a" "answer-5fbe3e02-0a60-5155-aaa9-1099c2486ac5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1dd3b9ac-3e11-5981-a4d8-309f740a2b9a" :answer/id #uuid "1dd3b9ac-3e11-5981-a4d8-309f740a2b9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c9718c7-902f-5345-ad03-482984e9c1fe" :answer/id #uuid "0c9718c7-902f-5345-ad03-482984e9c1fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea847776-7f1b-5b89-bb47-fd8b7fc0ef23" :answer/id #uuid "ea847776-7f1b-5b89-bb47-fd8b7fc0ef23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-635832eb-ba37-5e03-b2a0-da170625a38a" :answer/id #uuid "635832eb-ba37-5e03-b2a0-da170625a38a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5fbe3e02-0a60-5155-aaa9-1099c2486ac5" :answer/id #uuid "5fbe3e02-0a60-5155-aaa9-1099c2486ac5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-da6b0f51-7da3-5f92-8b12-f21abc3a1502" :question/id #uuid "da6b0f51-7da3-5f92-8b12-f21abc3a1502" :question/math-academy-id "q-149729" :question/problem "Suppose the following data is sampled from a population. Compute an estimate for the population mean.\n\n$$\n13,\\,12,\\,9,\\,3\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population with the population mean $\\mu .$ \nThen, the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{X}_{i}.\n$$\n\nNote that:\n\n- $\\overset{―}{X}$ is the mean value of ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n},$ while $\\overset{¯}{x}$ is the mean of a specific sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$\n\n- the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ is an estimator of the population mean $\\mu ,$ and\n\n- the value $\\overset{^}{\\mu }=\\overset{¯}{x}$ is an estimate of the population mean $\\mu .$\n\nTherefore, our estimate for the population mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{\\mu } & =\\overset{―}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(13+12+9+3) \\\\  & =\\frac{37}{4} \\\\  & =9.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-967125f4-f40d-593b-92b5-aa4cbabd7b80"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-967125f4-f40d-593b-92b5-aa4cbabd7b80" :answer-field/id #uuid "967125f4-f40d-593b-92b5-aa4cbabd7b80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e28998a7-4d68-5d5a-a55b-33ee2914774d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-05b86b9d-3da6-5793-a9a2-ff8597d2d88f" "answer-bee938dd-06c2-5f9c-8ef9-0f8d393a8280" "answer-64662eb3-5019-553c-8275-382223e2cb35" "answer-e37df5d9-6f3f-5219-8dd9-a68efc7b5e0c" "answer-e2